<section class="pub-card pub-section"><h2>How it works</h2><ol><li>For an article, choose “Publish in next weekly slot” in the editor. Existing topic, content and Founder Story approval checks still apply.</li><li>For social media, adapt the captions and media, save, review and approve the exact revision. Then choose “Queue in weekly channel slots”.</li><li>The next unoccupied slot is selected for each platform. Social posts linked to an article start at least 15 minutes after its publication time.</li><li>Automatic routes deliver where account permissions support them. Assisted routes create tasks; a reminder or upload acceptance is not proof of publication.</li></ol><p>Saving new preferences does not move existing scheduled items. To replace a scheduled release, cancel its local jobs, save an updated draft and approve a new revision before queuing it. A reviewed retry of a failed weekly job receives a new weekly slot. Ambiguous outcomes require platform reconciliation before retrying.</p><p class="muted">Weekly worker: <?=!empty($heartbeat['at'])?e((new DateTimeImmutable('@'.$heartbeat['at']))->setTimezone(comm_zone($cfg['timezone']))->format('j M Y H:i T')):'Not checked yet'?>.</p></section></main>